# W2: the hanging CONTROL. c2-packed-tp4-warm4-control is W1's profile with the warm OFF (QWEN_FAST_M3_REQUEST_WARM=0): one value apart. It must hang at the first engine build after
# concurrent4's packed phase: the 150 s build deadline fires, the stack shows synchronize_device from verifier_engine.py:291 (the rows=2 warm-up), and the log shows two 'Forcing argmax' lines then silence.
# If it hangs at a prefill segment or a replay instead, record it: the class reading changes. If W2 completes, the control did not reproduce: run W2 once more. Two non-hanging controls block any
# production use of W1's result, which is then 'no hang, cause not attributed'. OPTIONAL: its expected product is a hang (data); a hang here is a pass of the control.
# Duration (estimate): 15-25 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/warm4 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/warm4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or
# a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag, built by B0 from the pushed tp4/warm4 commit; the driver
# substitutes it in every template once the image is built. A later commit needs a new tag.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-warm4a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-warm4-control
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
